#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# expm1

#% text
# `expm1(x)` gives `exp(x) - 1`, computed so that it stays accurate when `x` is small.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# For machine reals near 0, `exp(x) - 1` loses the digits of `x` to cancellation; `expm1` keeps them.

#% item
# Exact and symbolic arguments other than 0 stay unevaluated; `n` gives a number.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
expm1(1.0e-10)
#% output
#= 1.00000000005e-10

#% cell
exp(1.0e-10) - 1
#% output
#= 1.000000082740371e-10

#% cell
expm1(0)
#% output
#= 0

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A numerical value of an exact argument:

#% cell
n(expm1(log(2)))
#% output
#= 1.0

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `exp`, `log1p`, `n`
